A viable native Track B family does exist, but it is not the triage proposal. Proposition 3.1 makes “find/check \(r_f\)” essentially a table lookup, while Theorem 3.4 and Corollary 3.7 support a better task: compute the exact PBW normal form of a factored noncommutative polynomial. The reference scan is linear in every displayed coefficient; the planted permutation symmetry collapses it to three coefficient sums and three modular powers, with a fixed six-term polynomial answer. I’m implementing that distinction explicitly as Track B.
