The local construction has now passed an independent brute-force expansion check on eight demo seeds, in addition to its own optimized verifier. I found and fixed one robustness defect: certain mathematically valid-looking parameter combinations (for example `GF(11)` with exponent 10) could make the sampler loop forever because the power map had too few distinct nonunit images. Those combinations now fail immediately with a precise `ValueError`; preset behavior is unchanged.
