The bare run produced decisive feedback: every easy, medium, and configured hard attempt was solved exactly (9/9 total). The old construction’s repeated row multisets were too transparent, and merely adding more repeated rows would not grow the post-insight difficulty. I’m replacing that leak with a paper-native invariant tied to the displayed permutation \(f\): independently sampled coefficient rows will balance across \(f\)’s 2-cycles, so the reference PBW scan remains tens of thousands of operations while the compact route uses one cycle pair per branch.
