 ## Caveats
 
-- This is deliberately not a complexity-theoretic hardness claim. Any script can solve hard in milliseconds; Track B measures discovery of the compression without tools.
-- The 0/200,000 estimate samples the strongest freely deducible bounded prior used here—three independent nonzero branch scalars. It measures guessability, not resistance to algebraic analysis.
-- A multiset sort/hash attack would expose the invariant and solve every instance. That is the intended tool-assisted route, not a failing attack; the reference scan already establishes that efficient computation exists.
-- The hard renderer is about 75,000 characters. Although the answer and post-insight arithmetic meet G9(c), failure may partly reflect attention over a large coefficient table; the missing oracle run is therefore especially important.
-- `canonical_key` intentionally forgets cross-row column alignment after recording every row multiset and terminal coefficient multiset. This is invariant under all tested semantic symmetries and separates 20/20 unrelated seeds, but it can over-collapse adversarial non-generator inputs sharing those invariants.
-- No SAT/SMT, Gröbner-basis package, or external CAS attack was run. Those would be unnecessary overkill for this PBW presentation and would succeed, consistently with Track B.
-- `gvlib` is imported when available as required by the repository interface, but this family needs only standard-library modular integer arithmetic and degrades cleanly when `gvlib` is absent.
+- This is not a complexity-theoretic claim. Exact software solves it in
+  milliseconds; Track B concerns discovering compression without tools.
+- The 0/200,000 estimate samples the strongest freely deducible output prior:
+  three independent nonzero power-image scalars, with support and proportionality
+  already enforced. It measures guessing, not resistance to algebraic analysis.
+- A script that tests sums along `f`-cycles exposes the invariant immediately.
+  That is the intended tool-assisted route, not an omitted hardness claim.
+- The hard renderer is about 146,000 characters. Although the answer and
+  post-insight work meet G9(c), a future model failure could partly reflect
+  attention over the coefficient table; valid oracle arms are needed to diagnose it.
+- The canonical key preserves every row’s multiset of coefficient pairs along
+  `f`-cycles, terminal coefficients, and pivot/support incidence. It is invariant
+  under all tested semantic symmetries and separates 20/20 seeds, but may
+  over-collapse adversarial nongenerator inputs with identical invariants.
+- No external CAS or Gröbner-basis package was run; both would succeed and would
+  add no evidence for a Track B family. The required oracle panel remains blocked
+  solely by the exhausted OpenRouter key.
+- `gvlib` is imported when available but is not needed; the module remains
+  standard-library-only if it is absent.
