Completed a native Track B PBW-normal-form generator based on Theorem 3.4 and Corollary 3.6 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2308.11427v2).

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2308.11427/gen_2308_11427.py:1)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2308.11427/README.md:1)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2308.11427/selftest_report.json)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2308.11427/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2308.11427/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2308.11427/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Structured guessing: 0/200,000; exact probability \(1/1008^3\).
- Reference algorithm: 36,771 exact operations per shipping instance.
- Compact route: at most 51 operations.
- Oracle loop: easy 3/3 solved, medium 3/3 solved, hard 0/3 solved; verdict `hardened`.
- G9: bare 0/3, structural 3/3, placebo 2/3.

The current repository harness used its configured two-model pool. One hard failure was a length-limited empty response; this and the strong placebo effect are documented prominently in the README caveats.
